[(274, '2011-05-31 00:00:00', 28000.0, '{99109BBF-8693-4587-BC23-6036EC89E1BE}', '2011-04-16 00:00:00'), (274, '2011-08-31 00:00:00', 7000.0, '{DFD01444-8900-461C-8D6F-04598DAE01D4}', '2011-07-17 00:00:00'), (274, '2011-12-01 00:00:00', 91000.0, '{0A69F453-9689-4CCF-A08C-C644670F5668}', '2011-10-17 00:00:00')]
External knowledge that might be helpful: 
None
The table structure information is (table names): 
['salesperson', 'product', 'productmodelproductdescriptionculture', 'productdescription', 'productreview', 'productcategory', 'productsubcategory', 'salesorderdetail', 'salesorderheader', 'salesterritory', 'countryregioncurrency', 'currencyrate', 'SalesPersonQuotaHistory']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used

salesorderheader.salespersonid : link every sales order to a specific salesperson.  
salesorderheader.orderdate      : extract the calendar year of each order.  
salesorderheader.totaldue       : dollar value of every order; will be summed to get annual sales.  

SalesPersonQuotaHistory.BusinessEntityID : identifies the same salesperson in the quota table.  
SalesPersonQuotaHistory.QuotaDate        : extract the calendar year of the quota.  
SalesPersonQuotaHistory.SalesQuota       : the quota amount that will be compared with sales totals.  

salesperson.businessentityid    : master list of salespeople; useful when we want to list everyone, even if they have no sales or no quota in a given year.  

Typical conditions we will need  
• Join salesorderheader.salespersonid  = SalesPersonQuotaHistory.BusinessEntityID (through an aggregated sub‑query).  
• Filter or group by year  →  strftime('%Y', orderdate)  /  strftime('%Y', QuotaDate).  
• Aggregate totals with SUM(totaldue) for sales and SUM(SalesQuota) for quotas.  
• Calculate the difference  (total_sales – total_quota).  
• LEFT JOIN so that we keep a row even when sales or quotas are missing.

Exploratory SQL queries (simple → complex)

```sql
-- 1. Distinct salesperson IDs that appear in sales orders
SELECT DISTINCT salespersonid
FROM salesorderheader
WHERE salespersonid IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct salesperson IDs that ever have a quota entry
SELECT DISTINCT BusinessEntityID
FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct order years to see the span of sales data
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS order_year
FROM salesorderheader
ORDER BY order_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Quick look at individual orders: salesperson, date, value
SELECT salespersonid,
       orderdate,
       totaldue
FROM salesorderheader
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Annual sales total per salesperson (no quotas yet)
SELECT salespersonid,
       strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS sales_year,
       SUM(totaldue)            AS total_sales
FROM salesorderheader
GROUP BY salespersonid, sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Annual quota total per salesperson (no sales yet)
SELECT BusinessEntityID            AS salespersonid,
       strftime('%Y', QuotaDate)   AS quota_year,
       SUM(SalesQuota)             AS total_quota
FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, quota_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine the two previous aggregates so we can see them side by side
WITH sales AS (
    SELECT salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS yr,
           SUM(totaldue)            AS total_sales
    FROM salesorderheader
    GROUP BY salespersonid, yr
),
quota AS (
    SELECT BusinessEntityID        AS salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', QuotaDate) AS yr,
           SUM(SalesQuota)          AS total_quota
    FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
    GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, yr
)
SELECT s.salespersonid,
       s.yr                         AS year,
       s.total_sales,
       q.total_quota
FROM   sales AS s
LEFT JOIN quota AS q
       ON q.salespersonid = s.salespersonid
      AND q.yr            = s.yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same join as #7 but include salespeople who have a quota even if they had no sales
WITH sales AS (
    SELECT salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS yr,
           SUM(totaldue)            AS total_sales
    FROM salesorderheader
    GROUP BY salespersonid, yr
),
quota AS (
    SELECT BusinessEntityID        AS salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', QuotaDate) AS yr,
           SUM(SalesQuota)          AS total_quota
    FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
    GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, yr
)
SELECT COALESCE(s.salespersonid, q.salespersonid) AS salespersonid,
       COALESCE(s.yr, q.yr)                       AS year,
       s.total_sales,
       q.total_quota
FROM quota AS q
LEFT JOIN sales AS s
       ON s.salespersonid = q.salespersonid
      AND s.yr            = q.yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Add the difference between sales and quota, keep every salesperson‑year that has either side
WITH sales AS (
    SELECT salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS yr,
           SUM(totaldue)            AS total_sales
    FROM salesorderheader
    GROUP BY salespersonid, yr
),
quota AS (
    SELECT BusinessEntityID        AS salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', QuotaDate) AS yr,
           SUM(SalesQuota)          AS total_quota
    FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
    GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, yr
)
SELECT COALESCE(s.salespersonid, q.salespersonid)        AS salespersonid,
       COALESCE(s.yr, q.yr)                              AS year,
       COALESCE(s.total_sales, 0)                        AS total_sales,
       COALESCE(q.total_quota, 0)                        AS total_quota,
       COALESCE(s.total_sales, 0) - COALESCE(q.total_quota, 0) AS sales_minus_quota
FROM sales AS s
FULL JOIN quota AS q
      ON q.salespersonid = s.salespersonid
     AND q.yr            = s.yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: difference between annual sales and quota for every salesperson‑year
WITH sales AS (
    SELECT salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS yr,
           SUM(totaldue)            AS total_sales
    FROM salesorderheader
    GROUP BY salespersonid, yr
),
quota AS (
    SELECT BusinessEntityID        AS salespersonid,
           strftime('%Y', QuotaDate) AS yr,
           SUM(SalesQuota)          AS total_quota
    FROM "SalesPersonQuotaHistory"
    GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, yr
)
SELECT sp.businessentityid                       AS salespersonid,
       yr                                        AS year,
       COALESCE(total_sales, 0)                  AS total_sales,
       COALESCE(total_quota, 0)                  AS total_quota,
       COALESCE(total_sales, 0) - COALESCE(total_quota, 0) AS difference
FROM   salesperson AS sp
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT COALESCE(s.salespersonid, q.salespersonid) AS salespersonid,
           COALESCE(s.yr, q.yr)                       AS yr,
           COALESCE(s.total_sales, 0)                 AS total_sales,
           COALESCE(q.total_quota, 0)                 AS total_quota
    FROM sales AS s
    FULL JOIN quota AS q
          ON q.salespersonid = s.salespersonid
         AND q.yr            = s.yr
) AS x
ON  x.salespersonid = sp.businessentityid
ORDER BY salespersonid, year
LIMIT 20;
```

